        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. THE CONTAGIOUS DISEASES (ANIMALS) ACT, 1894. THE SWINE FEVER ORDER OF 1908 (No. 7,447). CLEANSING AND DISINFECTING of Vans, Carts, or other Vehicles used by persons for carrying bwine, or of ropes, nets or other apparatus. CLEANSING AND DISINFECTING by Pig Dealers as hereinafter defined. I\IOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that Articles 11 and -LI 12 of the above Order provide as follows : Article 11. The floor of any van, cart or other vehicle used in connection with the trade or business of a pig-dealer for the conveyance of swine along any highway or thoroughfare, and all other parts thereof with which any mosneir pig or its droppings have come in of clealming contact shall be cleansed and disin- arid di sin- footed in manner prescribed by feeting is set Article 13 of this Order by and at the out in the expense of the person using the same foil owing for such purpose as soon as practicable Regulation. after such use and before being again used for such purpose, and also at any , time forthwith upon the receipt ef a Notice In writing signed by anl Inspector of the Board or of the Local Authority requiring such cleansing and disinfection. Article 12. Any orate, box, hamper, net, rope, i or other thing used by a pig dealer n connection with his trade or business of a pig dealer for the conyeyance of swine along any highway or thorough- fare or on a railway shall be cleansed Ths manner of deansing and disinfected in manner prescribed by Article 13 of this Order by and at et l and disen- the expense of the person using the ecting is s same for such purpose as soon as out in the practicable after such use and before f 01l owing Regulation. being again used for such purpose, and also at any time forthwith upon the receipt of a Notice in writing signed by an Inspector of the Board or of the Local Authority requiring such cleansing and disinfection. CLEANSING AND DISINFECTING by persons other than Pig Dealers. NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN that at a meeting of the Executive cfrbrnm:44o, or we Local Autuority or toe Louniy or Ckester held at Crewe on Friday, the 23rd day of October, 1908, IT WAS ORDERED that from and after the first day of January, 1909, the following Regulation be made as to the CLEANSING AND DISINFECTING OF VANS, CARTS, OR OTHER VEHICLES, &amp;0., used in the District of the Local Authority of the County of Chester BY PERSONS OTHER TITAN PIG DEALERS in the conveyance of Swine on land otherwise than on a railway, that is to say All Vans, Carte, or other Vehicles used by Persons not being Pig Dealers for carrying Swine on land otherwise than on a Railway, and also all ropes, nets or other apparatus used by such Persons in the conveyance of swine on land otherwise than on a Railway shall, WHENEVER REQUIRED BY AN INSPECTOR OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY under the above Act, _ _ _</p>
        <p>_ be thoroughly cleansed and disinfected in the manner prescribed by Article 13 of the Swine Fever Order of 1908 (No. 7,447), and which is as follows : MANNER OF CLEANSING AND DISINFECTION. Article 13—(1). Any part of a place or thing required by this Order to be cleansed and disinfected shall be cleansed and disinfected in manner following : (i). The part of a place or thing shall, if the nature theree so permit, be scraped, and, where necessary, swept, and the scrapings and sweepings and all dung, sawdust, litter and other matter Flail be effectually moved therefrom ; then— (ii). The part of a place or thing shall be thoroughly washed or scrubbed or rcoured with water ; then (iii). The part of a place or thing shall be thoroughly coated or washed with— (a) A one per cent (minimum) solution of chloride of lime conteining not less than thirty per cent of available chlorine ; or (b) a flee per cent (minimum) solution of carbolic acid (containing not less than ninety-live per cent of actual carbolic acid) followed by a thorough sprinkling with limewash ; or (c) a disinfectant equal in disinfective efficiency to the above-mentioned solution of carbolic acid, followed by a thorough sprinkling with limewash. (2). The scrapings and sweepings and the dung, sawdust, litter and other matter removed under this Article shall forthwith be well mixed with quicklime and be effectually removed from contact with swine. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council.</p>
        <p>Chester, 18th November, 1008. A "Pig Dealer " means a person habitually engaged in the trade or business of selling swine(other than swine bred by him), but does not include a person who, as auctioneer, sells swine which are the property of another person. Th e District of the Local Authority of the County of Chester for the purposes of the Contagious Diseases (Animals) Act, 1801, does not include the City of Chester or any of the Boroughs either wholly or partly within the County. PENALTIES.—Any offence against the above Order or Regulation is deemed an offence against the Act of 1894, which renders the offender liable to a penalty of not exceeding TWENTY POUNDS.</p>
