        <p>RUNCORN MAN'S FATAL CONTEMPT.</p>
        <p>HANDS, ARMS &amp; NECK ' CKED BY RAW, RUNNING SORES.</p>
        <p>TERRIBLE strain is put upon the skin when the weather sets in cold damp. The pores close up to keep out the :old, and the blood being driven inwards, the :in is starved for lack of nourishment and Ner-run with cracks and chafing, so imall one day as to produce merely an unpleasant roughness, but the next grown into un- sightly and painful eruptions which are a veritable o'pen invitation to skin-disease. , Bowen, f South Gentle anointings with that Queen of ~..ington London," W. Healing Balms, Zam-Buk, not only saves you from all winter skin-torture, but regularly used will conquer the worst form of eczema that the cold weather may already have provoked. Raw, Running Sores.—Miss Ethel Sowell, of Onslow Square, SouthSensington,London.W.. whose tender skin was seriously affected by a change of air. writes :—" A rash appeared on my arm which began to itch and b own terribly.. Matter oozed out through the raw flesh and soon my arm was a mass of scabs. The disease next broke out on my face and hands, especially etween the fingers. Medical treatment did no good, im I tried Zam-Buk. which soothed the inflamed skip, dried the sores up, and finally drove all disease away, leaving me with a healthy unblemished skin." Zant-Iluk is excellent for bad legs, ringworm, ulcers, piles, burns, scalds, sprains, chapped hands. gore feet. rheumatic pains and swellings, slam chafing, abscesses, sore lips, and all wounds that have taken "bad ways." -Of all chemists, 1174, 219, or 416 per box.</p>
