        <p>Bold-street Evangelistic Mission.</p>
        <p>There was an encouraging attendance at the mission service held in the Wesleyan Shboolroom on Sunday evening after the ordinary services in the church. Mr. It. 11. Sutton presided. A solo was rendered by Mr. Tonge, of Sankey Bridges, entitled" lie's knocking at my heart," Mr. Smiley led the devotional part, and the lesson was read by Mr. Dean. A helpful address was given by the Rev. F. Remick supplemented by an earnest appeal by Mr. Sutton in closing the service.</p>
