      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-12-12_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
        <head>Do YOU suffer from Lumbago? Dropsy? Urinary Disorders? Rheumatism? Dizziness? Pains in the Loins and Back?</head>
        <p>Do YOU suffer from Lumbago? Dropsy? Urinary Disorders? Rheu- matism? Dizziness? Pains in the Loins and Back?</p>
        <p>Nothing is more to be feared than uric acid poisoning, because it comes on so quietly, and is often unsuspected until it has spread dangerous disease throughout the body. The kidneys' great work is to filter the uric acid out of the blood. But when they are weak and ill they fall behind with their work, and so the blood, burdened with this dangerous poison, carries disease to all parts of the system. This explains how uric acid makes you always tired, impatient and irritable ---your back is bad ---your head throbs and aches and comes over dizzy--- the eyes are puffy, the skin yellow ----you have rheumatic pains in the muscles and joints. There may be urinary dis- orders, gravel, dropsy, gout and lumbago. How to get well is best told in the grateful words of the Warrington man who speaks here of Doan's Backache Kidney Pills,— for there's nothing so convincing as the personal experience of a neighbour.</p>
        <p>Mr. E. Oakley, 1, Bond-street, Sankey, War- rington, says : -" I used to be a sufferer from dropsy and kidney trouble ; my limbs swelled very much. I was subject to severe pains in the small of my back, hips and loins. I consulted a doctor, and he advised me to go into an infirmary. Altogether I was laid up for ten weeks, and I got no real benefit until I tried Doan's backache kidney pills. =an's pills are a splendid medicine, they have made me well again, and I shall take pleasure in speaking about them. (Signed) E. OAKLEY."</p>
        <p>After a lapse of more than e;ghteen, months, one of our representatives had the pleasure of seeing Mr. Oakley, who said : —" I have not needed to use Doan's backache kidney pills since they cured me so thoroughly- It was dropsy that I had : my body swelled considerably, and I was unable to pass the kidney secretions properly, which were unnatural in colour, painful in passing, and contained sediment ; Doan's pills, however, caused them to pass natur- ally. I was treatcd for kidney trouble at the hospital, where I remained a month ; twenty-one days in bed."</p>
        <p>Ofall chemists and storec, as. gd. per lo,x 6 boxes, xt. ad. ; or post free direct front Foster-McC'ellan Co.. 8. Wells-street, Oxford-street, London. W. Be sure you get the same kind of pills as Mr. Oakley had.</p>
