        <head>EXAMINATION DAY.</head>
        <p>EXAMINATION DAY.</p>
        <p>The inspector was examining Standard 1., and all the class had been specially told be- forehand by the master: Don't answer unless you are almost certain your answer is cor- rect." History was the subject dealt with. -" Now tell me," said the inspector, 'who was the mother of our great Scottish hero, Robert Bruce." He pointed to the top boy, then round the class. There was no. answer. Then at last the heart of the teacher leapt with joy. The boy who was standing at the very foot held up his hand. "Well, my boy," said the inspector, encouragingly. who was she " Please. sir, Mrs. Bruce." JAMES HESEY DONEY. _</p>
