        <p>COUNTY OF CHESTER. DISEASES OF ANIMALS ACT, 1894. SWINE FEVER ORDER OF 1908 (No. 7,447). KEEPING OF REGISTERS BY PIG DEALERS. NTOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that at a Meeting of _LI the Executive Committee of the Local Authority of the County of Chester, held at Crewe on Friday, the 23rd day of October, 1908, IT WAS ORDERED that from and after the drat day of January, 1909, the follow- ing Regulation be made with reference to the KEEPING OF REGISTERS BY PIG DEALERS RESIDENT IN THE DISTRICT OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITY OF THE COUNTY 01? CHESTER, and to remain in operation until modified or revoked, that Is to say : EVERY PERSON resident within the District of the Local Authority of the County of Chester and CARRYING ON THE TRADE OR BUSINESS OF A PIG DEALER shall keep A REGISTER in the form supplied by the Local Authority open to inspection at all reasonable times' by any Inspector of the Board of Agriculture and Fisheries, or an Inspector of the Local Authority,and shall correctly enter therein all information relating to the purchases and sales of Swine, and in particular the names and addresses of persons from whom the Swine were purchased and the numher and description thereof, and the date of purchase and the removal thereof, and shall also enter in such Register the name and address of the person or persons to whom all Swine purchased are sold, and the number, description, and date of removal thereof to the premises of the purchaser, and the whole of such entries shall be made in ink in such Register within forty-eight hours after each purchase or sale. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council, Chester, 18th November, 1908. A" Pig Dealer "means a person habitually engaged in the trade or business of selling Swine (other than Swine bred by him), but does not include a person who, as Auctioneer, sells swine which sre the property of another person. 1 The District of the Local Authority of the County of Chester for the purposes of the Contagious Diseases (Animals) Act, 1894, does not include the City of Chester or any of the Boroughs either wholly or partly within the County. I PENALTIES.—Any offence against the above Regulation is deemed an offence against the Act of 1894, 'which renders the offender liable to a penalty of not exceeding TWENTY POUNDS.</p>
