        <p>QUESTIONS know what benefit has accrued to inmates or ratepayers for the immoderate item of deputations and confer- FOR TARIFF REFORMERS ences of which Hr. A. J. Jolley has had the "lion's share " ? There must be a bottom to this business. We must 'aave an inquiry and report into this matter IX.—lf Import duties are not paid by egetreencilsinagnboelyvoonrdt opportunity includingforonctMo Councillor a years n exercise the home consumer, why do Pro- his peculiar gifts of inquiry, and of Hr. Furness to get tectionist nations grant "draw- further satisfied.—Yours respectfully, backs" of duties paid P JOHN HALEY Tariff Reformers" tell us that when we tax imports we " tax the foreigner." How is this to be reconciled with the "drawback " system ? Protectionist countries grant what is known as a " drawback " on the exportation of goods made from imported commodities upon which Customs duty has been paid— i.e., the import tax is refunded to the home consumer. It is thus recognised that the home user of the taxed material has paid the import tax. The United States, for example' has a big import tax on tinplates. When cans or drums made Out of imported tinplate are ex-ported by canning firms, the duty is refunded on the ground that it has I been actually paid by the user. L. G. C. DI.</p>
